M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"755ccbc641d955cfeab527ff326926a8bbee094a263e487c2654426a04648993","event_uuid":"bfc8eb78-85df-4191-bc21-7d9aa89bdf70","position":{"commit_sha":"83a44b7ae35782f912b1dcf4597781ada9d0d453","position":"1787575039293427001-bfc8eb78-85df-4191-bc21-7d9aa89bdf70"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787027843891965001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"dd336b50-a8f4-4248-a2b0-e43127fd2227","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"7bc2-5203-d5f4-4a4a"},{"link_uuid":"3306fa41-d639-4552-8c4d-52010786e4f8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"01ef-8903-1e56-4108"}],"description":"## Context\nCloud summary writes currently cross ACLI subprocess behavior and a shared REST helper that retries three times with 2s/5s waits. The selected route must consume only the shared logical budget without weakening unrelated callers.\n\n## Outcome\nImplement one Cloud summary write invocation and primary-store observation under the S1 contract. Each write launches one ACLI process; summary recovery performs one REST request with no inner sleep.\n\n## Plan\n1. Add sanitized historical exit/stdout/stderr fixtures, including the real exit-1 unauthorized shape, and fail loud on unknown shapes.\n2. Execute one `acli jira workitem edit` process per physical write invocation. Preserve POSIX process-group and non-POSIX child cleanup.\n3. Thread a per-call retry policy from `_rest_urlopen_with_retry` up through its sole GET intermediary `_direct_rest_get` (both in `acli_rest.py`) to `get_issue_by_rest`. `_rest_urlopen_with_retry` gains an optional policy argument defaulting to today's three attempts with 2s/5s backoff; `_direct_rest_get` gains a matching optional pass-through argument with the same default. Only `get_issue_by_rest`'s summary-recovery call selects the one-attempt/no-sleep policy. Every other consumer of `_direct_rest_get` keeps three attempts with 2s/5s waits unchanged by omitting the argument: `get_issue_property` and `search_user_by_email` (in `acli_rest.py`), the status-transitions read (`acli.py`), and the issuelinks read (`acli_graph.py`). The direct `_rest_urlopen_with_retry` callers that bypass `_direct_rest_get` (the PUT/POST helpers and paged GETs in `acli_rest.py`) likewise omit the argument and are unchanged. `get_issue_by_rest` (in `acli.py`) is itself a shared entry point with production consumers OUTSIDE the `jira/` adapter dir, so the policy is a per-call pass-through argument on `get_issue_by_rest` too, defaulting to today's three-attempt/2s-5s behavior and forwarded to `_direct_rest_get`. ONLY the new summary-recovery observation call passes the one-attempt/no-sleep policy; every other caller of `get_issue_by_rest` omits the argument and is byte-for-byte unchanged. Those callers are enumerated explicitly: `outbound_differ.py:132` (`client.get_issue_by_rest(jira_key)`), `apply_handlers.py:259` (`ctx.client.get_issue_by_rest(str(jira_key))`), and `binding_store.py:108` (resolved dynamically via `getattr(client, \"get_issue_by_rest\", None)`). None of these three changes call signature or retry posture — each keeps three attempts with 2s/5s waits, and the pre-existing HTTP-error-not-retried contract that `outbound_differ.py:127` documents is untouched because the policy governs only connection-level retry, not HTTP-error handling.\n4. Classify auth/TLS/permission/invalid requests as permanent; eligible network, 429, and retryable 5xx outcomes return metadata to the shared budget rather than replaying locally.\n5. Observe the primary REST issue resource, never indexed ACLI JQL, before any ambiguous replay.\n6. Emit exactly one redacted completion log for every terminal/exhausted outcome or cleanup failure. Include only logical id, disposition, invocation count, request count, cleanup status, `retry_not_before`, and one redacted message capped at 512 Unicode code points; cap the whole serialized log at 1,024 Unicode code points.\n\n## Testing\nStateful fakes and real child-process tests assert process/request counts, cleanup, classification, redaction, exact completion-log fields and bounds, one-log emission cardinality, and neighbor retry behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] One Cloud write invocation launches exactly one ACLI process.\n- [x] Summary recovery performs one primary-store REST request with no inner sleep or JQL.\n- [x] All unrelated REST callers retain three attempts with 2s/5s waits, verified for each `_direct_rest_get` sibling (`get_issue_property`, `search_user_by_email`, transitions read, issuelinks read), the direct PUT/POST callers, AND every existing `get_issue_by_rest` consumer outside the `jira/` adapter dir — `outbound_differ.py:132`, `apply_handlers.py:259`, and `binding_store.py:108` (via `getattr`) — each of which omits the policy argument and is asserted to retain the three-attempt/2s-5s default; only the summary-recovery call selects the one-attempt/no-sleep path.\n- [x] Permanent and transient outcome classes map to the shared contract without adapter replay.\n- [x] Historical triples decode deterministically and unknown triples do not retry.\n- [x] Timeout cleanup passes for POSIX process groups and non-POSIX child processes.\n- [x] Operation diagnostics hold at most eight entries and every message is redacted before its 512-Unicode-code-point cap.\n- [x] Every terminal/exhausted outcome or cleanup failure emits exactly one completion log with only logical id, disposition, invocation/request counts, cleanup status, `retry_not_before`, and one redacted message capped at 512 Unicode code points; the whole log is at most 1,024 Unicode code points.\n\n## Out of scope\nCore dispatch cutover and Jira DC execution.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py","reason":"Expose the selected Cloud summary write and observation."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py","reason":"One-process invocation, outcome decoding, timeout, and cleanup."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_rest.py","reason":"Per-call single-attempt observation while preserving neighbor retry defaults."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/backend.py","reason":"Expose the typed Cloud operation."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/summary_operation.py","reason":"New Cloud summary operation module: execute/observe/classify/completion-log (acli.py is at the 800-LOC cap, so the operation logic lives in a dedicated module)."},{"path":"tests/fixtures/reconciler/rp03_acli_outcomes.json","reason":"Sanitized historical ACLI outcome corpus."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_jira_cloud_summary_operation.py","reason":"Cloud stateful operation, classification, completion-log, and request-count tests."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_t2_cloud_summary_operation_heldout.py","reason":"Held-out oracle pinning the Cloud summary operation core contract (policy pass-through, one-request observation, classification, completion log)."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_acli_subprocess_timeout.py","reason":"Cross-platform process cleanup regressions."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_acli_auth_failure.py","reason":"Historical unauthorized output regression."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","7bc2-5203-d5f4-4a4a"],["parent","f5ac-6373-5e33-4374"],["relates_